      "content": "International organizations like the UN are fundamentally designed to prioritize global consensus over national sovereignty, which inevitably allows powerful nations to block or dilute the specific interests of smaller states. Their reliance on voting mechanisms means that any single nation's unique needs can be easily overridden by a coalition of major powers who have more leverage to shape outcomes. Furthermore, these bodies often lack the enforcement power to act decisively, turning them into bureaucratic hurdles rather than protective shields for individual countries. Ultimately, the very structure of these institutions sacrifices national autonomy for the sake of political compromise, making them ineffective guardians of specific national interests.",
